<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  HeadSetForFA_Revive.xml                    Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  THE BUG
  =======
  Head Set For [NL] Facial Animation dies in its static constructor on every
  single launch, and has done since before we started measuring:

      Error in static constructor of HeadSetForFA.HSMCache:
        TypeInitializationException, caused by NullReferenceException
        at HeadSetForFA.HSMSetting.CheckSettingData (Verse.ThingDef raceDef) [0x001c3]
        at HeadSetForFA.HSMSetting.InitializeData ()

  ROOT CAUSE  [VERIFIED FROM IL 2026-08-10]
  =========================================
  HSMCache's cctor builds a list of every ThingDef that is category=Pawn, has
  FacialAnimation.HeadControllerComp, and a non-null race. InitializeData()
  then calls CheckSettingData() on each. That method looks up a matching
  FacialAnimation.FaceAdjustmentDef by RaceName, and if the race has non-empty
  lifeStageAges it walks the adjustment def's AgeBasedParams list:

      IL_0184  ldloc.2 ; brfalse IL_025f     ; fad == null -> skip, safe
      IL_01c3  ldloc.s 9                     ; <== the reported offset
      IL_01c5  ldloc.2
      IL_01c6  ldfld    FaceAdjustmentDef::AgeBasedParams
      IL_01cb  callvirt List`1::get_Count    ; NRE when AgeBasedParams is null

  FaceAdjustmentDef's constructor initialises RaceName, both eye labels and the
  four Offset vectors, but NEVER initialises AgeBasedParams. So any adjustment
  def whose XML omits <AgeBasedParams> leaves the field null, and the first race
  it matches with life stages kills the whole mod.

  THE OFFENDING DEF  [VERIFIED 2026-08-10]
  ========================================
  A sweep of all 45,525 XML files across the 562 active mods found exactly THREE
  FaceAdjustmentDefs in the entire load set, and exactly one that can crash:

    DefaultFaceSizeAndPositionDef   RaceName ""      no AgeBasedParams  harmless
                                    (empty name matches no race)
    HumanFaceSizeAndPositionDef     RaceName Human   HAS AgeBasedParams safe
    BS_InsectoidHumanoid_FourArmed_FaceAdjustment    NO  AgeBasedParams CRASHES

  The last one is created at runtime by Facial Animation Compatability Project
  (danzinagri.facialanimationcompatabilityproject, load 550) in
  1.6/Patches/BS_Insectoid_FacialAnimation.xml. The same file also adds
  HeadControllerComp to BS_InsectoidHumanoid_FourArmed, so it supplies both
  halves of the trap. That race is ParentName="Human" and inherits Human's four
  life stages, so the lifeStageAges branch is taken and the null is hit.

  Note the crashing def is on the FA side. No race def is broken.

  THE FIX
  =======
  Give it an empty AgeBasedParams list. Count == 0 means the loop body never
  runs, `match` stays null, and CheckSettingData falls through to the branch
  that copies the def-level Size/Offset values into HSMData, which is the
  intended behaviour for a def with no age-based overrides.

  Deliberately using the explicit open/close form rather than a self-closing
  tag, so RimWorld's list parser produces an empty List rather than null.

  WHAT THIS DOES *NOT* FIX  [read before hoping]
  ==============================================
  This will NOT restore alien eyes or head shapes. HeadSetForFA only does FA
  head size/offset tuning per race and life stage, plus a per-xenotype FA
  on/off list. It never touches Verse.HeadTypeDef and never touches eye nodes.

  The real causes of the appearance problem are elsewhere and are separate:
    * EYES  : FA's own setting DrawEyesParts defaults to FALSE, and
              FacialAnimation.HarmonyPatches::Prefix_AddChild returns false for
              any PawnRenderNodeProperties_Eye node while it is off. Fix is the
              "Eyes" checkbox in FA's mod settings, not XML.
    * HEADS : FacialAnimation.HarmonyPatches::PostfixParallelPreDraw REMOVES the
              PawnRenderNode_Head draw request outright and paints its own face,
              so <forcedHeadTypes> can never render while FA draws that pawn.

  This patch is therefore hygiene: it removes a permanent every-launch static
  constructor failure and restores per-race head sizing. Worth doing on its own
  merits; not the appearance fix.

  ⚠️ It also switches on four dormant Harmony patches across a 562-mod stack.
  That is a real, if modest, behaviour change. If head sizes or offsets look
  wrong after this, this patch is the first thing to suspect.

  LOAD ORDER
  ==========
  The target def does not exist on disk. It is created by the compat project's
  patch at load 550, and we are 562 (last), so we apply after it. As with
  BiomeAnimalDanglingRefs_Fix, validate_patch.py will report 0 on-disk matches
  for these xpaths. That is expected, not a silent no-op.

  The test xpath and the inner xpath deliberately DIFFER here: we test for the
  absence of AgeBasedParams and add it to the parent. That is the legitimate
  add-if-missing shape, and it self-disables if the compat project ever ships
  the field.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * GONE: "Error in static constructor of HeadSetForFA.HSMCache"
    * That would leave ZERO dead mods in the load.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FacialAnimation.FaceAdjustmentDef[defName="BS_InsectoidHumanoid_FourArmed_FaceAdjustment"]/AgeBasedParams</xpath>
    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FacialAnimation.FaceAdjustmentDef[defName="BS_InsectoidHumanoid_FourArmed_FaceAdjustment"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <AgeBasedParams></AgeBasedParams>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
